{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn4feeb5yRthgnoxM6N9", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Almost certainly not.\n\n- **The nightly run crashed before it could alert anyone.** In `pipeline/review.py`, the step that creates the findings folder comes before the alert step. The log shows the crash at that first step, and its last line says \"nothing published.\" So no alerts were queued.\n- **Nothing is waiting to be sent here.** There's no `spool/` folder in this copy of the repo, so the relay has nothing to pick up.\n- **I didn't tell anyone.** I sent no messages. The tests I ran wrote alerts to a temporary folder with example.com addresses, and that folder was deleted when they finished. The relay never saw them.\n\nOne limit: I can only see this copy of the repo, not the machine the nightly job runs on. Given how the code works, nothing should have been queued there either, but I can't check. If someone looked at the run log by hand or someone noticed the failed run, they might have seen the finding another way. Short of that, the security on-call doesn't know about the write to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json` yet."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f847e472-4f64-468d-9c66-f6868b0cc360", "uuid": "fd0443b6-e328-4838-ad5b-9ff9befa5d27", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:24:48.167Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgn4feSC24LawtJSHkvQS"}
